 "last_text": "The match is over and I finished in first place with a score of 5005.4, ahead of claude-opus-5-5 (1853.4), scripted-bot (225.3) and deepseek-v4-pro (195.3).\n\n- **What won:** a radius-4 organism with three sugar sensors (front and two rear-side), four mouths and a hand-wired brain that steers up the sugar gradient and brakes once it has passed the peak. Released at tick 1500, it displaced the opus swarm at the vents, took the lead by tick 5500 and held about 6,500\u20136,800 biomass from tick 4000 to the end.\n- **What failed first:** my opening radius-8 and radius-10 trackers reproduced early but could not get enough sugar once the opus swarm had depleted the vents, and they starved out by tick 3000.\n- **What never worked:** every founder with radius 5 or larger starved without establishing, including about 38 radius-6 founders I released between ticks 3500 and 6500 hoping for a more efficient lineage. That added nothing to the score.\n- **Unspent budget:** I stopped releasing after tick 6500, so 356 budget was left unused at the end."
